<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia says wants OPEC quota rolled over.</title>
<headline>Indonesia says wants OPEC quota rolled over.</headline>
<dateline>DENPASAR, Indonesia 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian Mines and Energy Minister Ida Bagus Sudjana said on Thursday that he would call for maintaining production quotas at the annual ministerial meeting of the Organisation of Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC) in June this year.</p>
<p>&quot;Indonesia wants OPEC to roll-over the quota at the meeting,&quot; he told reporters while on a campaign tour for the May 29 general elections.</p>
<p>&quot;If the quota is raised, oil prices will fall,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>OPEC oil ministers are to meet in Vienna in June to discuss the quota.</p>
<p>OPEC has currently set a 25.03 million barrels per day (bpd) quota but production hit 26.90 million bpd in March, according to a Reuters survey.</p>
</text>
